    {
      "abstract": "This dataset contains the fundamental models and simulation data used in this research, and is divided into two parts: (1) The three-dimensional hydrodynamic mesh models and computational input files for the proposed T-shaped floating offshore wind turbine platform and the reference platform (VolturnUS-S) established using ANSYS AQWA; (2) The time-domain motion response simulation data of the VolturnUS-S platform under various environmental conditions (e.g., normal operating condition, extreme parked condition, and different wave headings). This dataset can be used to verify the multi-objective optimization design results of the novel T-shaped platform and to compare the motion performance differences between the two platforms under combined wind, wave, and current loads.",
